# S1771 -- epimorphisms of finite etale K-algebras and direct summands

Task: fill PreGaloisCategory.monoInducesIsoOnDirectSummand for
FiniteEtaleAlg K = (CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale K)^op, or report the exact missing
statement without sorry/fake.

## What is proved in this file (kernel checked, no sorry)

1. algEquiv_prod_quotient_of_isCompl: if I, J are ideals of a commutative
   K-algebra B with I + J = 1 and I ∩ J = 0, then B is isomorphic as a
   K-algebra to B/I × B/J (Chinese remainder theorem for the pair, upgraded
   to an algebra equivalence).

2. exists_prod_algEquiv_of_surjective: every surjective map
   f : B →ₐ[K] A of finite etale K-algebras is the first projection of a
   direct product decomposition

     ∃ C, ∃ e : B ≃ₐ[K] A × C, f = fst.comp e.toAlgHom.

   The proof is the idempotent splitting: a finite etale K-algebra is reduced
   and Artinian, hence a semisimple ring; in a semisimple ring every ideal is
   generated by an idempotent (IsSemisimpleRing.ideal_eq_span_idempotent), so
   the complement J of ker f satisfies J * J = J; then B/J is formally etale
   over B (Algebra.FormallyEtale.iff_of_surjective), finite over K, hence
   finite etale over K, and the Chinese remainder theorem for the complete
   pair of ideals (ker f, J) gives the product decomposition.

3. The main target is reduced to two precise missing statements, recorded as
   the Props EpiSurjectiveField and ProductFanLimitField:

   * EpiSurjectiveField: every epimorphism in the category of finite etale
     K-algebras is surjective;
   * ProductFanLimitField: the binary fan given by a product decomposition
     B ≃ₐ[K] A × C is a limit in the full subcategory of finite etale
     K-algebras (the categorical product is the Pi algebra; the ambient limit
     is available, the statement for the full subcategory in the form needed
     here is formal transport and should be obtainable from
     createsLimitFullSubcategoryInclusion').

4. monoInducesIsoOnDirectSummand_of_missing: conditional main theorem: if
   EpiSurjectiveField and ProductFanLimitField hold, then
   MonoInducesIsoOnDirectSummandField holds for FiniteEtaleAlg K.

## Exact mathematical content of the missing statements

EpiSurjectiveField is the only genuinely mathematical gap.  A complete proof
runs as follows.  Let f : B → A be an epimorphism of finite etale K-algebras.
  * By Algebra.Etale.iff_exists_algEquiv_prod, A ≃ₐ[K] ∏ i, A i and
    B ≃ₐ[K] ∏ j, B j with all A i, B j finite separable field extensions of K.
    A K-algebra map ∏ j, B j → A i factors through one projection
    B j → A i (an idempotent argument; exists_factor in S1747Probe9.lean).
  * If f is not surjective, then either two factors of A come from the same
    factor of B, or one of the field maps B j → A i is not an isomorphism onto
    A i.  In both cases one builds two distinct maps g₁, g₂ : A → R to a
    suitable finite etale K-algebra R (a tensor product A i ⊗_{B j} A i resp.
    A i ⊗_{B j} A i', or a finite Galois extension of K containing the
    relevant fields) which agree after precomposing with f; this contradicts
    that f is an epimorphism.
  * Hence f is surjective, and exists_prod_algEquiv_of_surjective splits it.

An alternative route for the same lemma is Stacks 04VM (an epimorphism of
rings that is integral is surjective), together with the fact that B is finite
(hence integral) over K; Mathlib has the finite version in
RingHom.surjective_of_epi_of_finite but only for epimorphisms in the ambient
category CommRingCat, not for the full subcategory of finite etale algebras.

ProductFanLimitField is purely bookkeeping/transport: the fan is a limit in
CommAlgCat K (Pi product), the cone point B is finite etale, and the inclusion
of a full subcategory reflects limits whose cone point lies in the
subcategory (proof: a cone in the subcategory is a cone in the ambient
category; the ambient limit lift is a morphism between objects of the
subcategory, hence a morphism of the subcategory, and uniqueness transfers).

No sorry is used in this file.  The two missing statements occur only as
explicit hypotheses of the conditional theorem, never as axioms.
-/

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace S1771FiniteEtaleEpiSplit

variable {K : Type u} [Field K]

/-! ### 1. Chinese remainder theorem for a complete pair of ideals -/

/-- If I + J = 1 and I ∩ J = 0 for ideals of a commutative K-algebra B,
then B is isomorphic as a K-algebra to B/I × B/J. -/
noncomputable def algEquiv_prod_quotient_of_isCompl {B : Type u} [CommRing B] [Algebra K B]
    (I J : Ideal B) (h : IsCompl I J) :
    B ≃ₐ[K] ((B ⧸ I) × (B ⧸ J)) := by
  have hcop : IsCoprime I J := Ideal.isCoprime_iff_sup_eq.mpr h.sup_eq_top
  let φ : B →ₐ[K] ((B ⧸ I) × (B ⧸ J)) :=
    AlgHom.prod (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ K I) (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ K J)
  have hcomp : (fun b : B => φ b) =
      fun b => (Ideal.quotientInfEquivQuotientProd I J hcop)
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ⊓ J) b) := by
    funext b
    ext
    · simp [φ, Ideal.quotientInfEquivQuotientProd_fst]
    · simp [φ, Ideal.quotientInfEquivQuotientProd_snd]
  have hmk : Function.Bijective (fun b : B => Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ⊓ J) b) := by
    rw [h.inf_eq_bot]
    convert (AlgEquiv.quotientBot K B).symm.bijective using 1
    ext b
    simp
  have hbij : Function.Bijective φ := by
    change Function.Bijective (fun b => φ b)
    rw [hcomp]
    exact (Ideal.quotientInfEquivQuotientProd I J hcop).bijective.comp hmk
  exact AlgEquiv.ofBijective φ hbij

@[simp]
lemma algEquiv_prod_quotient_of_isCompl_apply {B : Type u} [CommRing B] [Algebra K B]
    (I J : Ideal B) (h : IsCompl I J) (b : B) :
    algEquiv_prod_quotient_of_isCompl (K := K) I J h b =
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk I b, Ideal.Quotient.mk J b) := rfl

/-! ### 2. A surjective map of finite etale K-algebras is a product projection -/

/-- Every surjective map of finite etale K-algebras is the first projection of
a product decomposition B ≃ₐ[K] A × C. -/
noncomputable def exists_prod_algEquiv_of_surjective
    (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra K A] [Module.Finite K A] [Algebra.Etale K A]
    [CommRing B] [Algebra K B] [Module.Finite K B] [Algebra.Etale K B]
    (f : B →ₐ[K] A) (hf : Function.Surjective f) :
    ∃ (C : Type u) (_ : CommRing C) (_ : Algebra K C) (_ : Module.Finite K C)
      (_ : Algebra.Etale K C),
      ∃ e : B ≃ₐ[K] (A × C), f = (AlgHom.fst K A C).comp e.toAlgHom := by
  haveI : IsReduced B := Algebra.FormallyUnramified.isReduced_of_field K B
  haveI : IsArtinianRing B := IsArtinianRing.of_finite K B
  haveI : IsSemisimpleRing B := IsArtinianRing.isSemisimpleRing_of_isReduced B
  let I : Ideal B := RingHom.ker f
  obtain ⟨J, hJ⟩ := ComplementedLattice.exists_isCompl I
  obtain ⟨eJ, heJ, hJe⟩ := IsSemisimpleRing.ideal_eq_span_idempotent J
  have hJidem : IsIdempotentElem J := by
    rw [hJe]
    simp [IsIdempotentElem, Ideal.span_singleton_mul_span_singleton, heJ.eq]
  haveI hFE : Algebra.FormallyEtale B (B ⧸ J) := by
    refine (Algebra.FormallyEtale.iff_of_surjective (R := B) (S := B ⧸ J) ?_).mpr ?_
    · simpa [Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq] using Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (I := J)
    · have hker : RingHom.ker (algebraMap B (B ⧸ J)) = J := by
        simpa [Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq] using Ideal.mk_ker (I := J)
      rwa [hker]
  haveI hFEK : Algebra.FormallyEtale K (B ⧸ J) := Algebra.FormallyEtale.comp K B (B ⧸ J)
  haveI hFinC : Module.Finite K (B ⧸ J) := Module.Finite.quotient K J
  have hEtC : Algebra.Etale K (B ⧸ J) := by
    refine ⟨hFEK, ?_⟩
    exact (Algebra.FinitePresentation.of_finiteType (R := K)).mp inferInstance
  let crt : B ≃ₐ[K] ((B ⧸ I) × (B ⧸ J)) :=
    algEquiv_prod_quotient_of_isCompl (K := K) I J hJ
  let q : (B ⧸ I) ≃ₐ[K] A := Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hf
  let ee : B ≃ₐ[K] (A × (B ⧸ J)) :=
    crt.trans (AlgEquiv.prodCongr q (AlgEquiv.refl : (B ⧸ J) ≃ₐ[K] (B ⧸ J)))
  refine ⟨B ⧸ J, inferInstance, inferInstance, hFinC, hEtC, ee, ?_⟩
  have crt_apply : ∀ b : B, crt b = (Ideal.Quotient.mk I b, Ideal.Quotient.mk J b) :=
    algEquiv_prod_quotient_of_isCompl_apply (K := K) I J hJ
  have ee_apply : ∀ b : B, ee b = (f b, Ideal.Quotient.mk J b) := by
    intro b
    change (AlgEquiv.prodCongr q (AlgEquiv.refl : (B ⧸ J) ≃ₐ[K] (B ⧸ J))) (crt b) = _
    rw [crt_apply]
    simp only [AlgEquiv.prodCongr_apply, Equiv.prodCongr_apply, Prod.map_apply]
    have hq : q (Ideal.Quotient.mk I b) = f b :=
      Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective_mk hf b
    exact Prod.ext hq rfl
  ext b
  change f b = (ee b).1
  rw [ee_apply]

/-! ### 3. The opposite category and the target field -/

/-- The opposite of the category of finite etale K-algebras. -/
abbrev FiniteEtaleAlg (K : Type u) [Field K] : Type (u + 1) := (CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.{u} K)ᵒᵖ

/-- The target: every monomorphism in (FiniteEtale K)^op induces an isomorphism
on a direct summand (Lenstra (G3)). -/
def MonoInducesIsoOnDirectSummandField (K : Type u) [Field K] : Prop :=
  ∀ {X Y : FiniteEtaleAlg K} (i : X ⟶ Y), Mono i →
    ∃ (Z : FiniteEtaleAlg K) (u : Z ⟶ Y),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (BinaryCofan.mk i u))

/-! ### 4. The two precise missing statements -/

/-- MISSING (M1) -- every epimorphism of finite etale K-algebras is a
surjective algebra map.

This is the only genuine mathematical gap.  See the module docstring for the
full proof (product of finite separable fields; an epimorphism that is not
surjective is separated by two maps to a finite etale algebra; alternatively
Stacks 04VM in the ambient category). -/
def EpiSurjectiveField (K : Type u) [Field K] : Prop :=
  ∀ {X Y : CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.{u} K} (f : X ⟶ Y), Epi f →
    Function.Surjective (fun x : X => f.hom.hom x)

/-- MISSING (M2) -- the binary fan of a product decomposition is a limit in
the full subcategory CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale K of finite etale algebras.

The corresponding fan is a limit in the ambient category CommAlgCat K (the Pi
algebra is the categorical product).  Because the cone point B is finite
etale, the ambient limit is also a limit in the full subcategory; Mathlib's
createsLimitFullSubcategoryInclusion' is designed for exactly this transport
and the remaining work is formal. -/
def ProductFanLimitField (K : Type u) [Field K] : Prop :=
  ∀ {A B C : Type u} [CommRing A] [Algebra K A] [Module.Finite K A] [Algebra.Etale K A]
    [CommRing B] [Algebra K B] [Module.Finite K B] [Algebra.Etale K B]
    [CommRing C] [Algebra K C] [Module.Finite K C] [Algebra.Etale K C]
    (e : B ≃ₐ[K] (A × C)),
    Nonempty (IsLimit (BinaryFan.mk
      (CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.ofHom ((AlgHom.fst K A C).comp e.toAlgHom))
      (CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.ofHom ((AlgHom.snd K A C).comp e.toAlgHom))))

/-! ### 5. Conditional main theorem -/

/-- Conditional main theorem. Assuming (M1) every epimorphism of finite etale
K-algebras is surjective, and (M2) the product fan is a limit in the full
subcategory, the direct-summand axiom holds for (FiniteEtale K)^op.

This is the exact reduction of the task: the remaining gap is precisely
EpiSurjectiveField ∧ ProductFanLimitField. -/
theorem monoInducesIsoOnDirectSummand_of_missing
    (hEpi : EpiSurjectiveField K) (hProd : ProductFanLimitField K) :
    MonoInducesIsoOnDirectSummandField K := by
  intro X Y i hi
  have hE : Epi i.unop := inferInstance
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (fun x : Y.unop => i.unop.hom.hom x) :=
    hEpi i.unop hE
  obtain ⟨C, hCR, hAlg, hFin, hEt, e, he⟩ :=
    exists_prod_algEquiv_of_surjective (K := K) X.unop Y.unop i.unop.hom.hom hsurj
  let g : Y.unop →ₐ[K] C := (AlgHom.snd K X.unop C).comp e.toAlgHom
  let Z : FiniteEtaleAlg K := Opposite.op (CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.of K C)
  let u : Z ⟶ Y := (CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.ofHom g).op
  refine ⟨Z, u, ?_⟩
  have hiunop : i.unop = ObjectProperty.homMk (CommAlgCat.ofHom (i.unop.hom.hom)) := by
    apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    exact (CommAlgCat.ofHom_hom i.unop.hom).symm
  have hfan : BinaryFan.mk i.unop u.unop =
      BinaryFan.mk
        (CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.ofHom ((AlgHom.fst K X.unop C).comp e.toAlgHom))
        (CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.ofHom ((AlgHom.snd K X.unop C).comp e.toAlgHom)) := by
    rw [hiunop]
    change BinaryFan.mk (CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.ofHom (i.unop.hom.hom))
      (CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.ofHom g) = _
    rw [he]
  have hlim : IsLimit (BinaryFan.mk i.unop u.unop) := by
    rw [hfan]
    exact (hProd e).some
  exact ⟨by simpa using BinaryFan.IsLimit.op hlim⟩

/-! ### 6. Axiom audit -/

#print axioms S1771FiniteEtaleEpiSplit.algEquiv_prod_quotient_of_isCompl
#print axioms S1771FiniteEtaleEpiSplit.algEquiv_prod_quotient_of_isCompl_apply
#print axioms S1771FiniteEtaleEpiSplit.exists_prod_algEquiv_of_surjective
#print axioms S1771FiniteEtaleEpiSplit.monoInducesIsoOnDirectSummand_of_missing

end S1771FiniteEtaleEpiSplit
